---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../../components/Diagram.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const S = "server/src/iki_server/entities/services.py";
const E = "server/src/iki_server/entities/entries.py";
const M = "server/src/iki_server/entities/models.py";

const reg = [
  { id: "registry", x: 20, y: 30, w: 220, h: 64, label: "Registry", sub: "every project is in one" },
  { id: "entryb", x: 300, y: 30, w: 240, h: 64, label: "Entry", sub: ["the identity: hash, facts,", "values the identity decides"], strong: true },
  { id: "reca", x: 160, y: 160, w: 220, h: 64, label: "Project A's record", sub: "its own fields, accession, HRID" },
  { id: "recb", x: 460, y: 160, w: 220, h: 64, label: "Project B's record", sub: "its own fields, accession, HRID" },
  { id: "registrar", x: 600, y: 30, w: 160, h: 64, label: "Registrars", sub: "curate, supersede" },
];
const regEdges = [
  { from: "registry", to: "entryb", label: "holds" },
  { from: "reca", to: "entryb", label: "entry" },
  { from: "recb", to: "entryb", label: "entry" },
  { from: "registrar", to: "entryb", label: "facts", dashed: true },
];

const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: "What a thing is, and what a project knows of it" },
  { id: "how", label: "Entries, records and registrars" },
  { id: "hrids", label: "HRIDs" },
  { id: "rules", label: "The rules in full" },
  { id: "ref", label: "Routes, files and decisions" },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title="What a thing is, and what a project knows of it">
    <p>
      A type with an <code>identity</code> is registered. What a thing is lives once per registry,
      as an <strong>entry</strong>: the identity, the facts about it, and the values the identity
      alone decides. Each project that has it keeps its own <strong>record</strong> of it, pointing
      to the entry and sharing its HRID, with everything that depends on how that project made or
      measured it, accessions included. Registrars curate an entry's facts and supersede a mistaken
      entry (<Adr n={[115, 131, 143, 154]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title="Entries, records and registrars">
    <Diagram id="reg" title="An entry and its projects' records" width={780} height={240} boxes={reg} edges={regEdges}>
      <div slot="registry">
        <p>Every project is in one registry; registries and their registrars are org models.</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/org/models.py" sym="class Registry(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/org/models.py" sym="class Registrar(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="entryb">
        <p>
          An <code>iki_entity</code> row with a registry, no project, and an identity hash:
          canonical JSON of the identity fields, naming the type, hashed with SHA-256. Database
          constraints keep one entry per identity per registry, and one record per entry per
          project.
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/identity.py" sym="def identity_hash(" />, <Path p={M} sym="iki_entity_identity_once" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="reca">
        <p>A record has an owner project and an entry. A value is <code>registry: derived</code> only if the identity alone determines it; anything a run's parameters change is the record's (<Adr n="0131" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={M} sym="iki_entity_record_once" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="recb">
        <p>An accession (a UniProt ID, say) is the record's, not the entry's: two projects may have it from different sources (<Adr n="0154" />).</p>
      </div>
      <div slot="registrar">
        <p>A holder sets a fact while it's empty; after that only the registry's registrars change it, with a reason. An identity field never changes: a registrar supersedes the entry instead (<Adr n="0143" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={E} sym="def curate(" />, <Path p={E} sym="def supersede(" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>
    <p>
      <strong>Registering.</strong> A create of a type with an identity hashes the identity, takes
      an advisory lock on the registry and that digest, and looks for the entry. If there's none it
      makes one, then the project's record. If there is one, what the create says about the entry
      fills what it hasn't got, and a fact that differs is refused; a project that already has a
      record of it gets that record back, as <code>reused</code>. Two people registering the same
      thing at once make one entry: the second waits, then finds it (<Path p={S} sym="def _find_entry(" />).
      The full order is on <PageLink to="Saving and validation" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Which fields go where.</strong> A field marked <code>registry: derived</code> is set
      once at registration (a formula, a weight, a canonical form). One marked <code
        >registry: fact</code
      > is a curated fact the identity doesn't determine (a CAS number, an INN). Everything else is
      the project's record's. An identity reads sequences and sets of parts as what they are, so
      the same molecule spelled two ways is one entry (<Adr n="0138" />).
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>References to an identity name its entry</strong>: the foreign key is to the entries'
      table. When a project reads the reference, it's titled by that project's own record of the
      entry where it has one. <PageLink to="Links between records" /> covers how references are read.
    </p>

    <h3 id="hrids">HRIDs</h3>
    <p>
      A human-readable ID, such as <code>PRT-000123</code>, comes from one Postgres sequence per
      prefix (<code>iki_hrid_prt</code>). <code>sync_plugins</code> creates the sequences and never
      drops them, so a number is never handed out twice, even if a plugin is removed and comes back.
      Numbers outgrow their padding rather than wrap. A project's record of an entry takes the
      entry's HRID, so every project calls the same thing by the same ID (<Path
        p="server/src/iki_server/entities/hrids.py"
        sym="def next_hrid("
      />). The app's database role can move a sequence forward past a number an import kept, through{" "}
      <code>iki_hrid_advance</code>, and do nothing else to it (<Path
        p="server/src/iki_server/core/db_roles.py"
        sym="iki_hrid_advance"
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title="The rules in full">
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Superseding and moving" open>
        <p>
          A registrar replaces a mistaken entry (drawn with the wrong stereochemistry, say) with
          another of the same type in the same registry, with a reason. It can't be undone. The
          superseded entry is kept, marked, and can't be registered again; the people who added
          each holding project's record, and those projects' Admins, are told. A holder's Editor
          then moves the project's record to the replacement: it keeps its data, history and runs,
          and the project's own references to the old entry are re-pointed, each a revision with the
          reason (<Path p={E} sym="def move(" />). A locked record can't be moved.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="What a registrar sees">
        <p>
          A registrar sees the entry: its values, its history, and how many projects hold it, never
          which, nor their records. An entry's revision made through a project the reader can't read
          says what it set, never who, how or when.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="An entry has no states">
        <p>
          States, locks and archiving are the project's record's. An entry isn't archived: its
          registrars supersede it. Its facts' changes are <code>curated</code> revisions, and the
          holders are told.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADRs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0035" />'s <code>on_duplicate</code> was removed by <Adr n="0115" />: a project has at most one record of each entry.</li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title="Routes, files and decisions">
    <Routes tags={["registries"]} />
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Where</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Path p={E} />: curating, superseding, moving</li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/entities/identity.py" />: an identity's digest</li>
          <li><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/identity.py" />: the hash</li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/entities/hrids.py" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0115" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0131" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0138" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0143" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0154" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0165" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
